---
// Links between the data levels of Tutorial3: MC tracks, MC points, digis and hits of one entry.
// Hover, tap or focus an object: the diagram lights up its chain back to the MC track, and the panel
// lists the links of the object as FairLink(file, entry, type, index), in the order of GetLinks().
// Select an MC track: the diagram lights up the objects that link to it.
//
// Facts and where they come from (paths relative to the FairRoot repository):
// - A FairLink has a file, an entry, a type, an index and a weight. File -1: the current file. Entry -1: the current
//   entry. Type: the branch, -1 if not set. Index: the position in the container of the branch
//   (fairroot/base/event/FairLink.h:13-19). The default link is (-1, -1, -1, -1), weight 1: fFile and fType store
//   the value + 1 (FairLink.h:122-183). FairLink(branchName, ...) gets the type from
//   FairRootManager::GetBranchId() (fairroot/base/event/FairLink.cxx:19-38).
// - Following a link, FairRootManager::GetCloneOfLinkData() takes the input tree for file -1, the current entry for
//   entry -1, the branch GetBranchName(type), and the element `index` of its TClonesArray
//   (fairroot/base/steer/FairRootManager.cxx:497-577).
// - Branch ID = the position of the name in fBranchNameList (FairRootManager.cxx:264-277). Register() adds the names
//   in the order of the calls (FairRootManager.cxx:172-173, 185-196). The list goes to the file as "BranchList"
//   (FairRootManager.cxx:383-390), and FairFileSource::Init() adds the list of the input first
//   (fairroot/base/source/FairFileSource.cxx:189-207), so the IDs stay the same in the next run.
// - IDs of the Tutorial3 chain (examples/advanced/Tutorial3/macro/run_sim.C, run_digi.C, run_reco.C):
//   run_sim.C:110 calls SetStoreTraj(kTRUE). FairMCApplication::InitGeometry() calls FairTrajFilter::Init(), which
//   registers "GeoTracks", before RegisterOutput() (fairroot/base/sim/FairMCApplication.cxx:857-875,
//   fairroot/base/steer/FairTrajFilter.cxx:78-81, FairTrajFilter.h:119). RegisterOutput() registers "MCTrack"
//   (examples/common/mcstack/FairStack.cxx:315-322), "FairTestDetectorPoint" (Tutorial3/simulation/FairTestDetector.cxx:122-131)
//   and "MCEventHeader." (FairMCApplication.cxx:945-978, fairroot/base/event/FairMCEventHeader.cxx:82-85).
//   So: 0 GeoTracks, 1 MCTrack, 2 FairTestDetectorPoint, 3 MCEventHeader.
//   run_digi.C: FairRunAna::Init() reads the input list (fairroot/base/steer/FairRunAna.cxx:142), registers
//   "EventHeader." (185-204, fairroot/base/event/FairEventHeader.cxx:17-20), then calls InitTask() (238):
//   FairTestDetectorDigiTask::Init() registers "FairTestDetectorDigi" (Tutorial3/digitization/FairTestDetectorDigiTask.cxx:47-48).
//   So: 4 EventHeader., 5 FairTestDetectorDigi. run_reco.C: "EventHeader." is already in the list;
//   FairTestDetectorRecoTask::Init() registers "FairTestDetectorHit" (Tutorial3/reconstruction/FairTestDetectorRecoTask.cxx:51-52): 6.
// - Links on: the three macros call SetUseFairLinks(kTRUE) (run_sim.C:49, run_digi.C:50, run_reco.C:46;
//   FairRun.cxx:170). FairMultiLinkedData_Interface makes the set of links only then (FairMultiLinkedData_Interface.cxx:64-75).
// - Classes: FairTestDetectorPoint : FairMCPoint : FairMultiLinkedData_Interface (Tutorial3/data/FairTestDetectorPoint.h:16,
//   fairroot/base/event/FairMCPoint.h:21). FairTestDetectorDigi : FairTimeStamp : FairMultiLinkedData_Interface
//   (FairTestDetectorDigi.h:33, FairTimeStamp.h:22). FairTestDetectorHit : FairHit : FairTimeStamp (FairTestDetectorHit.h:24,
//   FairHit.h:22). FairMCTrack derives from TObject, so an MC track has no links (examples/common/mcstack/FairMCTrack.h:36).
// - MC point: FairTestDetector::AddHit() calls SetLink(FairLink(-1, fEventNr, GetBranchId("MCTrack"), trackID))
//   (FairTestDetector.cxx:153-169). At the end of the event FairMCApplication::FinishEvent() calls FillTrackArray() and
//   UpdateTrackIndex() (FairMCApplication.cxx:645-648); UpdateTrackIndex() calls point->SetLink(FairLink("MCTrack", newIndex))
//   (FairStack.cxx:280-294). SetLink() clears the set first (fairroot/base/event/FairMultiLinkedData.cxx:100-106).
//   So the stored link is (-1, -1, 1, index in MCTrack).
// - Digi: one digi for each point, at the index of the point, with
//   AddLink(FairLink(-1, GetEntryNr(), "FairTestDetectorPoint", ipnt)) (FairTestDetectorDigiTask.cxx:60-80).
//   GetEntryNr() is the entry that ReadEvent(i) reads (FairRootManager.cxx:409-416).
// - Hit: one hit for each digi, at the index of the digi, with
//   AddLink(FairLink(-1, GetEntryNr(), GetBranchId("FairTestDetectorDigi"), ipnt)) (FairTestDetectorRecoTask.cxx:62-85),
//   if fStreamProcessing is false, the default (fairroot/base/steer/FairTask.cxx:29).
// - History: AddLink() calls InsertLink() and, if fInsertHistory (default kTRUE, FairMultiLinkedData.cxx:25-33), also
//   InsertHistory(), which inserts the links of the target object (FairMultiLinkedData.cxx:117-183, 202-253). It does
//   not follow links to MCTrack or to another entry (214-219). So a digi holds 2 links and a hit holds 3.
// - Order: fLinks is a std::set<FairLink> (FairMultiLinkedData.h:135) with FairLink::operator<: file and entry count
//   only if both are not -1, then type, then index (FairLink.h:78-102). `less` below is the same rule. GetLink(i)
//   walks the set (FairMultiLinkedData.cxx:82-92). So the MC track link comes first.
// - Weight: 1 by default (FairLink.h:33-36). AddLink() multiplies it by mult = 1, and InsertLink() adds weights only
//   when the same link comes again (FairMultiLinkedData.cxx:117-120, 185-200). Here each link comes once: weight 1.
// - A type filter changes this: FairLinkManager::AddIncludeType() keeps only the listed types, and InsertLink() drops
//   the others (fairroot/base/steer/FairLinkManager.cxx:56-72, FairMultiLinkedData.cxx:187-189). run_digi.C:51 and
//   run_reco.C:47 call AddIncludeType(0). Type 0 is GeoTracks here, so with this filter the digis and the hits get no
//   links (InsertLink() also drops the copied ones). The diagram shows the links without the filter, and the caption says so.
// Example values, not from the code: entry 7, three MC tracks, five MC points, and the MC track of each point.

interface Lv {
  key: string;
  branch: string;
  type: number;
}
interface Link {
  f: number;
  e: number;
  t: number;
  i: number;
  to: string;
  how: string;
}
interface Obj {
  id: string;
  lv: number;
  i: number;
  src: string | null;
  trk: number;
  links: Link[];
  note: string;
}
interface Box {
  x: number;
  y: number;
  w: number;
  h: number;
}
interface Layout {
  id: 'wide' | 'narrow';
  W: number;
  H: number;
  box: Record<string, Box>;
  edge: (from: Box, to: Box) => { d: string; head: string };
}

const ENTRY = 7;
// The MC track of each MC point (example values).
const trackOf = [0, 0, 1, 2, 2];
const NT = 3;
const NP = trackOf.length;
const LV: Lv[] = [
  { key: 'trk', branch: 'MCTrack', type: 1 },
  { key: 'pnt', branch: 'FairTestDetectorPoint', type: 2 },
  { key: 'dig', branch: 'FairTestDetectorDigi', type: 5 },
  { key: 'hit', branch: 'FairTestDetectorHit', type: 6 },
];
const BRANCHES = ['GeoTracks', 'MCTrack', 'FairTestDetectorPoint', 'MCEventHeader.', 'EventHeader.', 'FairTestDetectorDigi', 'FairTestDetectorHit'];
const START = 'hit3';

const key = (lv: number, i: number) => `${LV[lv].key}${i}`;
const pointsOf = (t: number) => trackOf.flatMap((tr, i) => (tr === t ? [i] : []));

// FairLink::operator< (FairLink.h:78-102).
const less = (a: Link, b: Link) => {
  if (a.f !== -1 && b.f !== -1 && a.f !== b.f) return a.f < b.f;
  if (a.e !== -1 && b.e !== -1 && a.e !== b.e) return a.e < b.e;
  if (a.t !== b.t) return a.t < b.t;
  return a.i < b.i;
};
const setOrder = (ls: Link[]) => [...ls].sort((a, b) => (less(a, b) ? -1 : less(b, a) ? 1 : 0));
const L = (f: number, e: number, t: number, i: number, to: string, how: string): Link => ({ f, e, t, i, to, how });

// Text in backticks is code.
const O: Record<string, Obj> = {};
for (let t = 0; t < NT; t++) {
  const n = pointsOf(t).length * 3;
  O[key(0, t)] = {
    id: key(0, t),
    lv: 0,
    i: t,
    src: null,
    trk: t,
    links: [],
    note: `\`FairMCTrack\` derives from \`TObject\`. It has no links. ${n} objects link to it.`,
  };
}
for (let i = 0; i < NP; i++) {
  const t = trackOf[i];
  const toT = L(-1, -1, 1, t, key(0, t), 'history');
  O[key(1, i)] = {
    id: key(1, i),
    lv: 1,
    i,
    src: key(0, t),
    trk: t,
    links: [{ ...toT, how: 'SetLink()' }],
    note: '`FairTestDetector::AddHit()` sets a link to the MC track. At the end of the event, `FairStack::UpdateTrackIndex()` replaces it with the index in `MCTrack`.',
  };
  O[key(2, i)] = {
    id: key(2, i),
    lv: 2,
    i,
    src: key(1, i),
    trk: t,
    links: setOrder([L(-1, ENTRY, 2, i, key(1, i), 'AddLink()'), toT]),
    note: '`FairTestDetectorDigiTask::Exec()` adds the link to the point. `AddLink()` also copies the links of the point.',
  };
  O[key(3, i)] = {
    id: key(3, i),
    lv: 3,
    i,
    src: key(2, i),
    trk: t,
    links: setOrder([L(-1, ENTRY, 5, i, key(2, i), 'AddLink()'), L(-1, ENTRY, 2, i, key(1, i), 'history'), toT]),
    note: '`FairTestDetectorRecoTask::Exec()` adds the link to the digi. `AddLink()` also copies the links of the digi.',
  };
}
const ids = Object.keys(O);
const edges = ids.filter((k) => O[k].src).map((k) => [k, O[k].src!] as [string, string]);

// The chain of an object: the objects that its links point to. For an MC track: the objects that link to it.
// The number is the distance along the chain, for the delay of the highlight.
const chainOf = (id: string) => {
  const m = new Map<string, number>();
  const o = O[id];
  if (o.lv === 0) {
    for (const k of ids) if (k !== id && O[k].trk === o.trk) m.set(k, O[k].lv);
  } else {
    let c = o.src;
    let d = 1;
    while (c) {
      m.set(c, d++);
      c = O[c].src;
    }
  }
  return m;
};

const f1 = (n: number) => +n.toFixed(1);
const mean = (a: number[]) => a.reduce((s, v) => s + v, 0) / a.length;

// Wide: one column for each level, from left to right. A link goes to the left.
const wide = ((): Layout => {
  const W = 680;
  const BW = 56;
  const BH = 26;
  const top = 86;
  const pitch = 38;
  const cx = [92, 260, 430, 594];
  const box: Record<string, Box> = {};
  for (let lv = 1; lv < 4; lv++) for (let i = 0; i < NP; i++) box[key(lv, i)] = { x: cx[lv] - BW / 2, y: top + i * pitch, w: BW, h: BH };
  for (let t = 0; t < NT; t++) {
    const cy = mean(pointsOf(t).map((i) => top + i * pitch + BH / 2));
    box[key(0, t)] = { x: cx[0] - BW / 2, y: cy - BH / 2, w: BW, h: BH };
  }
  const H = top + (NP - 1) * pitch + BH + 16;
  const edge = (a: Box, b: Box) => {
    const x1 = a.x;
    const y1 = a.y + a.h / 2;
    const tx = b.x + b.w + 1.5;
    const ty = b.y + b.h / 2;
    const x2 = tx + 7;
    const xm = (x1 + x2) / 2;
    return {
      d: `M${f1(x1)} ${f1(y1)}C${f1(xm)} ${f1(y1)} ${f1(xm)} ${f1(ty)} ${f1(x2)} ${f1(ty)}`,
      head: `M${f1(tx)} ${f1(ty)}L${f1(x2)} ${f1(ty - 3.5)}L${f1(x2)} ${f1(ty + 3.5)}Z`,
    };
  };
  return { id: 'wide', W, H, box, edge };
})();

// Narrow (phones): one row for each level, from top to bottom. A link goes up.
const narrow = ((): Layout => {
  const W = 320;
  const BW = 26;
  const BH = 26;
  const gap = 5;
  const x0 = 162;
  const top = 36;
  const pitch = 60;
  const box: Record<string, Box> = {};
  const px = (i: number) => x0 + i * (BW + gap);
  for (let lv = 1; lv < 4; lv++) for (let i = 0; i < NP; i++) box[key(lv, i)] = { x: px(i), y: top + lv * pitch, w: BW, h: BH };
  for (let t = 0; t < NT; t++) {
    const cx = mean(pointsOf(t).map((i) => px(i) + BW / 2));
    box[key(0, t)] = { x: cx - BW / 2, y: top, w: BW, h: BH };
  }
  const H = top + 3 * pitch + BH + 12;
  const edge = (a: Box, b: Box) => {
    const x1 = a.x + a.w / 2;
    const y1 = a.y;
    const tx = b.x + b.w / 2;
    const ty = b.y + b.h + 1.5;
    const y2 = ty + 7;
    const ym = (y1 + y2) / 2;
    return {
      d: `M${f1(x1)} ${f1(y1)}C${f1(x1)} ${f1(ym)} ${f1(tx)} ${f1(ym)} ${f1(tx)} ${f1(y2)}`,
      head: `M${f1(tx)} ${f1(ty)}L${f1(tx - 3.5)} ${f1(y2)}L${f1(tx + 3.5)} ${f1(y2)}Z`,
    };
  };
  return { id: 'narrow', W, H, box, edge };
})();
const layouts = [wide, narrow];

// The first view shows hit 3. The script keeps the same state, so the page also works before it runs.
const chain0 = chainOf(START);
const isOn = (k: string) => chain0.has(k);
const edgeOn = (a: string, b: string) => (a === START || isOn(a)) && (b === START || isOn(b));
const o0 = O[START];
const fl = (l: Link) => `FairLink(${l.f}, ${l.e}, ${l.t}, ${l.i})`;
const nLinks = (n: number) => (n === 0 ? 'no links' : n === 1 ? '1 link' : `${n} links`);
const parts = (s: string) => s.split('`');
const typesOf = (id: string) => new Set(O[id].links.map((l) => l.t));
const t0 = typesOf(START);
const label = `Links of entry ${ENTRY} in Tutorial3: MC tracks, MC points, digis and hits. Each object is a button.`;
const data = JSON.stringify({ O, LV, start: START });
---

<figure class="fr-links not-content" data-links={data}>
  <div class="lk-head">
    <span class="lk-tip"
      ><span class="t-fine">Hover an object, or use the arrow keys, to see its links.</span><span class="t-touch"
        >Tap an object to see its links.</span
      ></span
    >
    <span class="lk-keys" aria-hidden="true">
      <span><i class="k-sel"></i>selected</span>
      <span><i class="k-on"></i>its chain</span>
      <span
        ><svg class="k-arr" viewBox="0 0 22 8" width="22" height="8"><path d="M22 4H6"></path><path d="M0 4L7 0.5V7.5Z"></path></svg
        >link</span
      >
    </span>
  </div>
  {
    layouts.map((Ly) => (
      <svg class={`lk lk-${Ly.id}`} viewBox={`0 0 ${Ly.W} ${Ly.H}`} role="group" aria-label={label}>
        {Ly.id === 'wide' ? (
          <g aria-hidden="true">
            <rect class="lk-band" x="6" y="50" width={Ly.W - 12} height={Ly.H - 56} rx="4" />
            <text class="lk-entry" x="16" y="69">
              entry {ENTRY}
            </text>
            {LV.map((lv, k) => {
              const b = Ly.box[key(k, 0)];
              const x = b.x + b.w / 2;
              return (
                <>
                  <text class="lk-br" x={x} y="20" text-anchor="middle">
                    {lv.branch}
                  </text>
                  <text class="lk-ty" x={x} y="38" text-anchor="middle">
                    type <tspan class="n">{lv.type}</tspan>
                  </text>
                </>
              );
            })}
          </g>
        ) : (
          <g aria-hidden="true">
            <rect class="lk-band" x="154" y="20" width={Ly.W - 156} height={Ly.H - 24} rx="4" />
            <text class="lk-entry" x={Ly.W - 6} y="13" text-anchor="end">
              entry {ENTRY}
            </text>
            {LV.map((lv, k) => {
              const b = Ly.box[key(k, 0)];
              return (
                <>
                  <text class="lk-br" x="4" y={b.y + 10}>
                    {lv.branch}
                  </text>
                  <text class="lk-ty" x="4" y={b.y + 25}>
                    type <tspan class="n">{lv.type}</tspan>
                  </text>
                </>
              );
            })}
          </g>
        )}
        <g aria-hidden="true">
          {edges.map(([a, b]) => {
            const e = Ly.edge(Ly.box[a], Ly.box[b]);
            return (
              <g class="lk-e">
                <path class="ln" d={e.d} />
                <path class="hd" d={e.head} />
              </g>
            );
          })}
        </g>
        {/* The chain: a copy of each link in a layer above, so that a grey link to the same object cannot cover it. */}
        <g aria-hidden="true">
          {edges.map(([a, b]) => {
            const e = Ly.edge(Ly.box[a], Ly.box[b]);
            const on = edgeOn(a, b);
            const d = on ? (chain0.get(b) ?? 0) - 0.5 : 0;
            return (
              <g class={`lk-e lk-hi${on ? ' is-on' : ''}`} data-edge={`${a} ${b}`} style={`--d:${d}`}>
                <path class="ln" d={e.d} />
                <path class="hd" d={e.head} />
              </g>
            );
          })}
        </g>
        <g>
          {ids.map((k) => {
            const b = Ly.box[k];
            const o = O[k];
            const cls = ['lk-b', k === START && 'is-sel', isOn(k) && 'is-on'].filter(Boolean).join(' ');
            return (
              <g
                class={cls}
                data-obj={k}
                role="button"
                tabindex={k === START ? 0 : -1}
                aria-pressed={String(k === START)}
                aria-label={`${LV[o.lv].branch} ${o.i}`}
                style={`--d:${chain0.get(k) ?? 0}`}
              >
                <rect class="ring" x={b.x - 3} y={b.y - 3} width={b.w + 6} height={b.h + 6} rx="5" />
                <rect class="bx" x={b.x} y={b.y} width={b.w} height={b.h} rx="3" />
                <text x={b.x + b.w / 2} y={b.y + b.h / 2 + 4.5} text-anchor="middle">
                  {o.i}
                </text>
              </g>
            );
          })}
        </g>
      </svg>
    ))
  }
  <div class="lk-panel">
    <p class="lk-ph">
      <code class="lk-name" data-name>{LV[o0.lv].branch}</code>
      <span class="lk-idx">index <b data-idx>{o0.i}</b></span>
      <span class="lk-count" data-count>{nLinks(o0.links.length)}</span>
    </p>
    <ul class="lk-list" data-list hidden={!o0.links.length}>
      {
        o0.links.map((l) => (
          <li>
            <code class="lk-fl">{fl(l)}</code>
            <span class="lk-to">
              → <code>{LV[O[l.to].lv].branch}</code> {O[l.to].i}
            </span>
            <span class={`lk-how${l.how === 'history' ? ' h' : ''}`}>{l.how}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p class="lk-note" data-note>{parts(o0.note).map((s, i) => (i % 2 ? <code>{s}</code> : s))}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="lk-legend">
    <p class="lk-lt"><code>FairLink(file, entry, type, index)</code></p>
    <dl class="lk-dl">
      <div><dt>file</dt><dd><code>-1</code>: the current file</dd></div>
      <div><dt>entry</dt><dd>the entry of the tree. <code>-1</code>: the current entry</dd></div>
      <div>
        <dt>type</dt>
        <dd>
          the branch ID: the position of the branch name in <code>BranchList</code>
          <span class="lk-chips">
            {
              BRANCHES.map((b, i) => (
                <span
                  class={['lk-chip', LV.some((l) => l.type === i) && 'lv', t0.has(i) && 'is-on', i === LV[o0.lv].type && 'is-sel']
                    .filter(Boolean)
                    .join(' ')}
                  data-type={i}
                >
                  <b>{i}</b>
                  {b}
                </span>
              ))
            }
          </span>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div><dt>index</dt><dd>the position in the <code>TClonesArray</code> of the branch</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
  <p class="lk-sr" aria-live="polite" data-live></p>
  <figcaption>
    Tutorial3 with <code>SetUseFairLinks(kTRUE)</code>, but without the type filter <code>AddIncludeType(0)</code> of <code>run_digi.C</code> and <code>run_reco.C</code>.
    Entry {ENTRY} and the indices are examples. Each link also has a weight, here 1.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
  interface LkLink {
    f: number;
    e: number;
    t: number;
    i: number;
    to: string;
    how: string;
  }
  interface LkObj {
    id: string;
    lv: number;
    i: number;
    src: string | null;
    trk: number;
    links: LkLink[];
    note: string;
  }
  interface LkData {
    O: Record<string, LkObj>;
    LV: { key: string; branch: string; type: number }[];
    start: string;
  }

  for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.fr-links')) {
    const { O, LV, start } = JSON.parse(root.dataset.links!) as LkData;
    const $ = <T extends Element>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const svgs = [...root.querySelectorAll<SVGSVGElement>('svg.lk')];
    const boxes = [...root.querySelectorAll<SVGGElement>('[data-obj]')];
    const edges = [...root.querySelectorAll<SVGGElement>('[data-edge]')];
    const chips = [...root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-type]')];
    const list = $<HTMLUListElement>('[data-list]');
    const live = $<HTMLElement>('[data-live]');
    const ids = Object.keys(O);
    const name = (id: string) => `${LV[O[id].lv].branch} ${O[id].i}`;
    const fl = (l: LkLink) => `FairLink(${l.f}, ${l.e}, ${l.t}, ${l.i})`;
    const nLinks = (n: number) => (n === 0 ? 'no links' : n === 1 ? '1 link' : `${n} links`);
    const code = (s: string) => {
      const c = document.createElement('code');
      c.textContent = s;
      return c;
    };
    // Text in backticks is code.
    const rich = (el: HTMLElement, text: string) => {
      el.replaceChildren();
      text.split('`').forEach((s, i) => {
        if (s) el.append(i % 2 ? code(s) : s);
      });
    };
    // The objects that the links of `id` point to, or for an MC track the objects that link to it,
    // with their distance along the chain.
    const chainOf = (id: string) => {
      const m = new Map<string, number>();
      const o = O[id];
      if (o.lv === 0) {
        for (const k of ids) if (k !== id && O[k].trk === o.trk) m.set(k, O[k].lv);
      } else {
        let c = o.src;
        let d = 1;
        while (c) {
          m.set(c, d++);
          c = O[c].src;
        }
      }
      return m;
    };

    let pinned = start;
    let shown = start;

    const show = (id: string) => {
      if (id === shown) return;
      shown = id;
      const o = O[id];
      const chain = chainOf(id);
      const inS = (k: string) => k === id || chain.has(k);
      for (const b of boxes) {
        const k = b.dataset.obj!;
        b.classList.toggle('is-sel', k === id);
        b.classList.toggle('is-on', chain.has(k));
        b.style.setProperty('--d', String(chain.get(k) ?? 0));
      }
      for (const e of edges) {
        const [a, b] = e.dataset.edge!.split(' ');
        const on = inS(a) && inS(b);
        e.classList.toggle('is-on', on);
        e.style.setProperty('--d', String(on ? (chain.get(b) ?? 0) - 0.5 : 0));
      }
      $('[data-name]').textContent = LV[o.lv].branch;
      $('[data-idx]').textContent = String(o.i);
      $('[data-count]').textContent = nLinks(o.links.length);
      list.replaceChildren(
        ...o.links.map((l) => {
          const li = document.createElement('li');
          const fc = code(fl(l));
          fc.className = 'lk-fl';
          const to = document.createElement('span');
          to.className = 'lk-to';
          to.append('→ ', code(LV[O[l.to].lv].branch), ` ${O[l.to].i}`);
          const how = document.createElement('span');
          how.className = `lk-how${l.how === 'history' ? ' h' : ''}`;
          how.textContent = l.how;
          li.append(fc, to, how);
          return li;
        })
      );
      list.hidden = !o.links.length;
      rich($<HTMLElement>('[data-note]'), o.note);
      const types = new Set(o.links.map((l) => l.t));
      for (const c of chips) {
        const t = Number(c.dataset.type);
        c.classList.toggle('is-on', types.has(t));
        c.classList.toggle('is-sel', t === LV[o.lv].type);
      }
    };

    const say = (id: string) => {
      const o = O[id];
      const ls = o.links.map((l) => `${fl(l)} to ${name(l.to)}, ${l.how === 'history' ? 'copied' : `from ${l.how}`}`);
      live.textContent = `${name(id)}: ${nLinks(o.links.length)}. ${ls.join('; ')}${ls.length ? '. ' : ''}${o.note.replace(/`/g, '')}`;
    };

    const pin = (id: string, focus = false) => {
      const changed = id !== pinned;
      pinned = id;
      for (const b of boxes) {
        const on = b.dataset.obj === id;
        b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(on));
        b.tabIndex = on ? 0 : -1;
      }
      if (focus) {
        // Only the boxes of the visible layout can take the focus.
        for (const b of boxes) if (b.dataset.obj === id && b.getClientRects().length) b.focus();
      }
      show(id);
      if (changed) say(id);
    };

    // Arrow keys go to the nearest box in that direction, in the same layout.
    const near = (from: SVGGElement, dx: number, dy: number) => {
      const own = boxes.filter((b) => b.ownerSVGElement === from.ownerSVGElement);
      const c = (b: SVGGElement) => {
        const r = b.getBoundingClientRect();
        return [r.left + r.width / 2, r.top + r.height / 2];
      };
      const [x0, y0] = c(from);
      let best: SVGGElement | null = null;
      let bs = Infinity;
      for (const b of own) {
        if (b === from) continue;
        const [x, y] = c(b);
        const along = (x - x0) * dx + (y - y0) * dy;
        if (along < 4) continue;
        const across = Math.abs((x - x0) * dy) + Math.abs((y - y0) * dx);
        const s = along + 3 * across;
        if (s < bs) {
          bs = s;
          best = b;
        }
      }
      return best;
    };

    for (const svg of svgs) {
      svg.addEventListener('keydown', (ev) => {
        const b = (ev.target as Element).closest<SVGGElement>('[data-obj]');
        if (!b || ev.altKey || ev.ctrlKey || ev.metaKey) return;
        const own = boxes.filter((x) => x.ownerSVGElement === svg);
        let to: SVGGElement | null = null;
        if (ev.key === 'ArrowRight') to = near(b, 1, 0);
        else if (ev.key === 'ArrowLeft') to = near(b, -1, 0);
        else if (ev.key === 'ArrowDown') to = near(b, 0, 1);
        else if (ev.key === 'ArrowUp') to = near(b, 0, -1);
        else if (ev.key === 'Home') to = own[0];
        else if (ev.key === 'End') to = own[own.length - 1];
        else if (ev.key === 'Enter' || ev.key === ' ') to = b;
        else return;
        ev.preventDefault();
        if (to) pin(to.dataset.obj!, true);
      });
      svg.addEventListener('pointerleave', (ev) => {
        if (ev.pointerType === 'mouse') show(pinned);
      });
    }
    for (const b of boxes) {
      b.addEventListener('pointerenter', (ev) => {
        if (ev.pointerType === 'mouse') show(b.dataset.obj!);
      });
      b.addEventListener('click', () => pin(b.dataset.obj!));
      b.addEventListener('focus', () => pin(b.dataset.obj!));
    }
  }
</script>

